# A stage0 sample whose recursion passes its bound. `countDown` prints its
# number and calls itself with the next one, stating `maxRecursion 4`; started at
# 1 it would stop at 6, but the fifth nested call traps (exit code 70) after
# printing 1 to 4. `refined run` and the executable stage0 builds from it
# stop at the same place.
depth is module
depth purpose "Recurse past a stated maxRecursion, so the bound's trap can be compared"
depth path depth
depth imports standard.console
depth imports standard.math
depth imports standard.compare
depth exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

countDown is operation
countDown purpose "Print a number, then count on from the next one until past the last, one call deeper each time"
countDown invariant none
countDown typeParameter none
countDown input number Int64 copied
countDown input last Int64 copied
countDown output none
countDown outputOwnedBy none
countDown raises none
countDown effect write console.stdout
countDown uses stdoutWriter
countDown memoryHeap false
countDown async false
countDown maxRecursion 4
countDown label begin loopKind none
countDown label begin within none
countDown label print loopKind none
countDown label print within none
countDown label printItDone loopKind none
countDown label printItDone within none
countDown label done loopKind none
countDown label done within none
countDown let one Int64 1 immutable
countDown at begin do pastCheck
countDown at begin branch if past goto done else goto print
countDown at print do printIt
countDown at print branch ifError printIt goto printItDone else goto printItDone
countDown at printItDone do next
countDown at printItDone do deeper
countDown at printItDone goto done
countDown at done return ok none

pastCheck is call
pastCheck in countDown
pastCheck invokes compare.greaterThanInt64
pastCheck argument left Int64 number copy
pastCheck argument right Int64 last copy
pastCheck result past Bool
pastCheck ownedBy none
pastCheck cleanedBy none
pastCheck borrows none
pastCheck catch none
pastCheck suppresses none

printIt is call
printIt rationale "The failure has nowhere to be reported, so it is discarded"
printIt in countDown
printIt invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printIt argument value Int64 number copy
printIt result none
printIt ownedBy none
printIt cleanedBy none
printIt borrows none
printIt catch printItError console.WriteError
printIt suppresses console.WriteError.failed

next is call
next in countDown
next invokes math.addInt64
next argument left Int64 number copy
next argument right Int64 one copy
next result following Int64
next ownedBy none
next cleanedBy none
next borrows none
next catch none
next suppresses none

deeper is call
deeper in countDown
deeper invokes countDown
deeper argument number Int64 following copy
deeper argument last Int64 last copy
deeper result none
deeper ownedBy none
deeper cleanedBy none
deeper borrows none
deeper catch none
deeper suppresses none

main is operation
main purpose "Count from 1 to 6 by recursion bounded to four nested calls"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap false
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable
main let one Int64 1 immutable
main let six Int64 6 immutable
main at begin do count
main at begin return ok okCode

count is call
count in main
count invokes countDown
count argument number Int64 one copy
count argument last Int64 six copy
count result none
count ownedBy none
count cleanedBy none
count borrows none
count catch none
count suppresses none
